1
00:00:00,860 --> 00:00:02,880
我们昨天得知了一个坏消息
We got some bad news yesterday.

2
00:00:03,580 --> 00:00:04,380
菲尔的妈妈去世了
Phil's mom died.

3
00:00:05,080 --> 00:00:06,460
倒也不是意料之外
It wasn't unexpected.

4
00:00:06,900 --> 00:00:07,920
菲尔陪在她身边
He was with her.

5
00:00:07,920 --> 00:00:10,300
她在睡梦中平静地走了
And she went very peacefully and asleep.

6
00:00:10,300 --> 00:00:11,880
我跟她有种特殊的感情
She and I had a special connection.

7
00:00:12,200 --> 00:00:13,140
我们都有
We all did.

8
00:00:13,320 --> 00:00:14,200
但主要是我
But mostly me.

9
00:00:14,660 --> 00:00:15,960
她说我和她很像
She said I was just like her.

10
00:00:15,960 --> 00:00:18,280
怎么 她也争强好胜到古怪的地步吗
What? Is she weirdly competitive too?

11
00:00:18,280 --> 00:00:20,760
明天全家人都要去佛罗里达
The whole family is going down to Florida tomorrow

12
00:00:20,760 --> 00:00:22,220
陪菲尔参加葬礼
to be with Phil for the service.

13
00:00:22,379 --> 00:00:23,686
真是莫大的安慰
Such a relieve.

14
00:00:23,760 --> 00:00:26,380
我能感觉到他现在是多么需要我
I can feel how much he needs me right now.

15
00:00:27,860 --> 00:00:29,240
终于来了
There they are.

16
00:00:30,460 --> 00:00:31,440
小家伙们好啊
Hey, guys.

17
00:00:32,969 --> 00:00:34,589
你把我的护颈枕都带来了
Oh, you brought my nap pillow.

18
00:00:34,600 --> 00:00:36,040
我好想你啊
I missed you so much.

19
00:00:37,140 --> 00:00:38,700
菲尔 我真遗憾
Phil, I'm so sorry.

20
00:00:39,500 --> 00:00:39,940
谢谢
Thanks.

21
00:00:40,120 --> 00:00:42,780
格蕾丝是个善良又古怪的女人
Grace was such a kind and whimsical soul.

22
00:00:42,900 --> 00:00:46,100
她给动物戴鹿角拍照片做成的圣诞贺卡
The different animals she put antlers on for christmas cards--

23
00:00:46,100 --> 00:00:46,700
太有创见了
Inspired.

24
00:00:46,960 --> 00:00:48,560
每张都是实拍 绝无PS伪造
Not a single one was photoshopped.

25
00:00:48,600 --> 00:00:49,600
鳄鱼的也是吗
Not even the alligator?

26
00:00:49,600 --> 00:00:50,900
害她被咬掉了小拇指尖
Cost her the tip of her pinkie,

27
00:00:50,900 --> 00:00:51,960
但她无怨无悔
but she had no regrets.

28
00:00:53,080 --> 00:00:54,340
你们能来我真的很高兴
I'm so glad you guys are here.

29
00:00:54,420 --> 00:00:56,200
希望请假没有让你为难
I hope it wasn't too hard to get away from work.

30
00:00:56,200 --> 00:00:57,983
不会 拜托 为家人做任何事都可以
No. Please, anything for family.

31
00:00:58,080 --> 00:01:00,100
能离开办公室 让我做任何事都可以
Anything to get me out of that office.

32
00:01:00,660 --> 00:01:03,440
无聊的文件 开不完的会
It's all boring paperwork and endless meetings.

33
00:01:04,040 --> 00:01:06,540
说真的 这场葬礼来得太是时候了
Honestly, this funeral could not have come at a better time.

34
00:01:06,860 --> 00:01:08,680
真会说话 你该把这句话写在花签上
Aw, that's sweet. You should put that on the flowers.

35
00:01:10,300 --> 00:01:11,920
歌洛莉亚 穿成这样一定很热吧
Gloria, you must be so hot in that.

36
00:01:12,120 --> 00:01:13,040
我这是服丧
I am in mourning.

37
00:01:13,040 --> 00:01:15,620
在哥伦比亚 丧礼是很严肃的事情
In Columbia, we take death very seriously.

38
00:01:15,620 --> 00:01:16,220
在哪儿不是呢
Where don't they?

39
00:01:16,240 --> 00:01:17,060
能把面纱摘了吗
Can we lose the veil?

40
00:01:17,220 --> 00:01:18,440
没有人要抓你 歌洛莉亚
Nobody's looking for you, Gloria.

41
00:01:18,700 --> 00:01:19,700
谁是歌洛莉亚
Who is Gloria?

42
00:01:20,240 --> 00:01:22,240
我在佛罗里达被通缉
I am a wanted woman in Florida.

43
00:01:22,560 --> 00:01:24,760
我曾在那里居住过 我离开时
I used to live there, and when I left,

44
00:01:24,760 --> 00:01:29,400
我的室友把我们的公寓改造成了妓院
my roommate made our apartment into a house of prostitution,

45
00:01:29,556 --> 00:01:31,260
而那时租约上留的还是我的名字
and my name was still on the lease.

46
00:01:31,260 --> 00:01:32,220
其实就跟个交通罚单差不多
It's like a traffic ticket.

47
00:01:32,220 --> 00:01:34,040
去趟法院 交个罚款 就完事儿了
You walk into court, pay a fine, it's done.

48
00:01:34,360 --> 00:01:35,020
"快速"又"简单"
Quick and easy.

49
00:01:35,020 --> 00:01:37,485
是啊 那家妓院就叫这名字
Yes, that was the name of the whorehouse.

50
00:01:38,120 --> 00:01:39,560
米奇尔 你能陪她上法院吗
Mitchell, can you go with her to court?

51
00:01:39,680 --> 00:01:41,180
她需要个像样点的律师
She's gonna need some sort of lawyer.

52
00:01:41,420 --> 00:01:43,480
杰 米奇尔现在真是疲惫不堪
Uh, you know, Jay, Mitchell is so burnt out right now.

53
00:01:43,480 --> 00:01:45,000
他十分需要休息
He is in desperate need of a break.

54
00:01:45,140 --> 00:01:47,240
法院传票不用脑子也能应付 拜托
Bench warrants are a no-brainer. And, I mean, come on.

55
00:01:47,260 --> 00:01:48,980
歌洛莉亚看起来像那种
Does Gloria really look like the kind of woman

56
00:01:48,980 --> 00:01:49,920
开妓院的女人吗
who would run a brothel?

57
00:01:52,522 --> 00:01:53,629
-我还是陪她去吧 -你还是去吧
- Yeah, I better go with her. - You should go.

58
00:02:01,560 --> 00:02:01,980
是啊
Yeah.

59
00:02:08,320 --> 00:02:09,880
你们来了
There they are!

60
00:02:11,207 --> 00:02:12,599
你真美 你好 克莱尔
Oh, you look beautiful. Hi, claire.

61
00:02:12,599 --> 00:02:13,851
你还好吗
How are you holding on, hmm?

62
00:02:13,851 --> 00:02:14,660
还好吧
Oh, well, you know...

63
00:02:14,660 --> 00:02:15,760
我们会挺过去的 对吧 老爸
We're getting through it. Huh, dad?

64
00:02:16,303 --> 00:02:18,372
我现在还好 就是有点失眠
Ah. I'm doing okay. A little trouble sleeping.

65
00:02:18,560 --> 00:02:19,720
我习惯她的鼾声了
I'm so used to her snoring,

66
00:02:19,720 --> 00:02:21,540
我可能得借一下邻居的牛头犬了
I may have to borrow the neighbor's bulldog.

67
00:02:23,227 --> 00:02:24,180
早上好 夏洛特
Morning, Charlotte!

68
00:02:24,180 --> 00:02:26,240
这是我从加州来的亲戚们
This is my family from California!

69
00:02:26,980 --> 00:02:29,840
看得出来 看起来都跟电影明星似的
I can tell. They all look like movie stars.

70
00:02:29,851 --> 00:02:30,818
谢谢
Ah. Oh, thank you.

71
00:02:30,934 --> 00:02:32,480
真奇怪 我认识那女人
That's nuts. I know that woman,

72
00:02:32,480 --> 00:02:33,980
但忘了在哪儿认识的
but I have no idea from where.

73
00:02:34,080 --> 00:02:36,020
是啊 这地方充满了这样的故事
Yeah. This place is full of stories like that.

74
00:02:38,120 --> 00:02:39,780
早上好 邓菲先生 客人们
Good morning, Mr. Dunphy, visitors.

75
00:02:39,940 --> 00:02:41,460
拜托 雪莉 叫我弗兰克就好了
Please, Shelley, call me Frank.

76
00:02:41,640 --> 00:02:42,120
不 先生
No, sir.

77
00:02:42,140 --> 00:02:44,260
可能"呼啸松"那边会这么称呼业主
That might be the way they do things at Whistling Pines,

78
00:02:44,280 --> 00:02:46,040
但我们"休闲园"的管理很规范严谨
But we run a tight ship here at Leisure Park.

79
00:02:46,420 --> 00:02:48,060
根据你的要求 我预订了
As per your request, I have reserved

80
00:02:48,060 --> 00:02:50,220
今晚的湖滨广场 时间为一小时
the lakeside promenade this evening for one hour,

81
00:02:50,231 --> 00:02:52,560
从下午5点开始 供您开追悼会
Beginning at 5:00 p.m., for your memorial service.

82
00:02:52,560 --> 00:02:54,560
顺便提醒您 广场上不能吸烟
May I remind you that there's no smoking on the grounds,

83
00:02:54,660 --> 00:02:56,440
湖边不能带玻璃制品 不能喂鸭子
no glass near the lake, no feeding the ducks?

84
00:02:56,440 --> 00:02:57,480
请您节哀顺变
And I'm sorry for your loss.

85
00:02:57,520 --> 00:02:59,580
-谢谢 -不能喂鸭子
- Thank you. - No feeding the ducks.

86
00:02:59,680 --> 00:03:01,400
你盯着我干什么
What are you looking at me for?

87
00:03:09,500 --> 00:03:10,720
我真喜欢这里
I love it here--

88
00:03:11,020 --> 00:03:12,020
修剪平整的草坪
manicured lawns,

89
00:03:12,020 --> 00:03:13,580
活动计划周详 晚餐及时
planned activities, early dinners.

90
00:03:13,840 --> 00:03:14,860
一个孩子还能要求什么呢
What more does a kid need?

91
00:03:15,080 --> 00:03:17,020
是啊 每个人都这么有礼貌又体贴
Oh, yeah. And everyone's so polite and considerate--

92
00:03:17,060 --> 00:03:19,180
不像基圈里那些无休止的明争暗斗
Nothing like the constant catfights in my circle,

93
00:03:19,180 --> 00:03:20,380
每一周
where every week,

94
00:03:20,380 --> 00:03:22,740
都有人会莫名其妙地生另一个人的气
somebody's mad at somebody for god knows who what,

95
00:03:22,740 --> 00:03:24,080
而我总是被卷入其中
and I'm always thrown into the middle.

96
00:03:24,400 --> 00:03:26,480
你好像很焦躁 他们这里有蒸汽房
You seem tense. You know, they have a steam room.

97
00:03:26,480 --> 00:03:27,800
要跟我一起出出汗吗
Wanna join me for a schvitz?

98
00:03:27,800 --> 00:03:28,520
拜托 这里可是佛罗里达
Please, it's Florida.

99
00:03:28,600 --> 00:03:30,240
我想流汗的话 只要动动胳膊就行了
If I wanna sweat more, I'll just move my arms.

100
00:03:30,280 --> 00:03:30,960
你去享受吧
You go have fun.

101
00:03:31,960 --> 00:03:32,680
嘿 你
Hey, you.

102
00:03:33,300 --> 00:03:34,460
你喜欢那本书吗
Are you liking that book?

103
00:03:34,600 --> 00:03:36,660
虽然这不是我在机场买过的最差劲的东西
Well, it's not the worst thing I've picked up at an airport,

104
00:03:36,660 --> 00:03:37,360
但也差不多了
but close.

105
00:03:37,880 --> 00:03:38,740
这是什么情况
What is this,

106
00:03:38,760 --> 00:03:40,640
是读书会还是选美大会啊
a book club or a Miss America Pageant?

107
00:03:42,620 --> 00:03:44,220
我们在找下一本要读的书
We're looking for our next book.

108
00:03:44,232 --> 00:03:45,340
你们现在读的是什么书
Oh, what are you reading now?

109
00:03:45,340 --> 00:03:46,980
《无辜香吻之诱惑》
"Tempted by her innocent kiss."

110
00:03:47,538 --> 00:03:48,780
你一定没听说过
I-I'm sure you don't know it.

111
00:03:48,780 --> 00:03:51,020
拜托 达文·卡特是艾希莉的第一个男人
Oh, please. Devon Carter was Ashley's first,

112
00:03:51,340 --> 00:03:52,780
她希望他们能激情永驻
she wants their passion to last,

113
00:03:52,880 --> 00:03:55,380
可当她发现他们的婚姻只是父亲的
but her hopes of true love are crushed when she finds out

114
00:03:55,380 --> 00:03:57,520
另一笔交易 她对于真爱的幻想破灭了
their marriage is just another one of daddy's business deals.

115
00:03:58,320 --> 00:03:58,980
我可是同性恋
I'm gay.

116
00:03:59,200 --> 00:04:01,240
我孙子也是同性恋
Oh! My grandson is gay.

117
00:04:01,320 --> 00:04:04,000
他叫丹尼尔·舒曼 你认识吗
His name is Daniel Schulman. Uh, do you know him?

118
00:04:04,040 --> 00:04:06,320
他是不是这么高 深色头发
Oh! Is he about this tall, dark hair,

119
00:04:06,320 --> 00:04:06,980
割过包皮
circumcised?

120
00:04:08,900 --> 00:04:09,380
你真坏
Terrible.

121
00:04:10,140 --> 00:04:11,580
不要紧张 好吗
Don't be nervous, all right?

122
00:04:11,580 --> 00:04:12,580
我会把你的情况说清楚
I'll explain your situation.

123
00:04:12,680 --> 00:04:13,660
很快就能离开这里了
We'll have you out of here in no time.

124
00:04:13,780 --> 00:04:15,540
县监狱关押30天
30 days in county jail.

125
00:04:16,640 --> 00:04:19,020
-什么 -她好强硬
- What? - Ooh, she's tough.

126
00:04:19,170 --> 00:04:20,518
下一个
Next.

127
00:04:20,980 --> 00:04:23,540
安妮塔·曼查卡 偷窃
Anita Menchaca. Petty theft.

128
00:04:24,920 --> 00:04:25,900
先生 您是律师吗
Mister, you're a lawyer?

129
00:04:26,140 --> 00:04:26,880
帮帮我 拜托了
Help me, please.

130
00:04:27,000 --> 00:04:28,280
不好意思 我是她的律师
Oh, I'm sorry. I'm her lawyer.

131
00:04:28,472 --> 00:04:31,136
不不 帮帮她 这样能进行得快一些
No, no, help her, so this will go faster.

132
00:04:31,691 --> 00:04:33,074
而且她让我想起了我外婆
And she reminds me of my abuela,

133
00:04:33,074 --> 00:04:36,353
她也带这样的头巾 也曾偷窃
with her head scarf and her petty theft charges.

134
00:04:37,080 --> 00:04:37,980
在这里 法官阁下
Here, your honor.

135
00:04:38,141 --> 00:04:40,213
我是米奇尔·普里契特 "曼查勾"小姐的律师
I'm mitchell pritchett, attorney to miss Manchego.

136
00:04:40,213 --> 00:04:41,199
-是曼查卡 -好的
- Menchaca. - Ah, yeah...

137
00:04:41,280 --> 00:04:43,140
你们准备好辩诉了吗
Are you ready to enter a plea?

138
00:04:43,700 --> 00:04:44,220
当然准备好了
Absolutely.

139
00:04:44,480 --> 00:04:46,120
我认为这种事件完全没有理由
I see no reason why this matter should

140
00:04:46,120 --> 00:04:48,060
占用更多贵法庭宝贵的时间了
take up any more of the court's valuable time.

141
00:04:48,680 --> 00:04:49,500
无罪 法官大人
Not guilty, your honor.

142
00:04:49,560 --> 00:04:49,920
为什么
Why?

143
00:04:51,720 --> 00:04:52,940
我需要点时间准备一下
Gonna need a minute.

144
00:04:58,580 --> 00:05:00,040
看我爸给了我什么
Look what my dad just gave me.

145
00:05:00,840 --> 00:05:02,340
拜托你告诉我盒子里装的不是你妈
Please tell me that's not your mom.

146
00:05:02,520 --> 00:05:04,040
不是 她已经给自己选好骨灰罐了
No, no. She picked out her own urn.

147
00:05:04,640 --> 00:05:05,480
我爸一直都说
My dad keeps saying

148
00:05:05,480 --> 00:05:07,560
那罐子小一码 不过她还是挤进去了
it's a size too small but she squeezed into it.

149
00:05:08,680 --> 00:05:10,780
这些东西是她留给孩子们的
No, this is stuff she left for the kids.

150
00:05:11,604 --> 00:05:13,168
-我能打开吗 -能啊
- Can I... open it? - Yeah.

151
00:05:13,920 --> 00:05:15,440
里面有张纸条是给你的
Wow. There's a note for you.

152
00:05:16,300 --> 00:05:17,760
我不敢看
I can't read it.

153
00:05:17,840 --> 00:05:18,500
-好吧 -你来好吗
- Okay. - Would you?

154
00:05:18,900 --> 00:05:19,780
好的
All right.

155
00:05:23,000 --> 00:05:23,420
"亲爱的菲尔
"Dear phil,

156
00:05:24,200 --> 00:05:26,440
你一直都是最棒的儿子
you've always been the most wonderful son,

157
00:05:26,440 --> 00:05:29,100
而我现在需要你为我做最后一件事"
and now I need you to do one last thing for me."

158
00:05:29,100 --> 00:05:29,720
不
Oh, no!

159
00:05:29,720 --> 00:05:32,160
她一定是让我把她的骨灰泼到牧师脸上
She's gonna ask me to throw her ashes in the pope's face.

160
00:05:33,680 --> 00:05:35,420
"不要告诉你父亲
"Don't say anything to your father

161
00:05:35,420 --> 00:05:36,740
因为他一定会反对
because he'll just resist,

162
00:05:36,760 --> 00:05:38,700
但是有一位名叫安妮·菲茨曼斯的女士
but there's a woman named Annie Fitzsimmons

163
00:05:38,700 --> 00:05:40,100
她就住在几条街外
who lives a few streets over.

164
00:05:40,420 --> 00:05:42,900
我们和她并不太熟 但我一向很欣赏她
We don't know her very well, but I've always admired her,

165
00:05:42,900 --> 00:05:45,120
我觉得她会和你父亲很般配
and I think she'd be perfect for your dad.

166
00:05:45,580 --> 00:05:46,820
因此 在你回家前
So before you go home,

167
00:05:46,820 --> 00:05:48,240
我希望你能撮合他们"
I want you to fix him up with her."

168
00:05:48,280 --> 00:05:49,360
这太疯狂了
That is crazy!

169
00:05:49,380 --> 00:05:50,560
"我知道这听起来很疯狂
"I know this sounds crazy,

170
00:05:50,740 --> 00:05:52,780
但这里的单身男士很紧俏
but single men are in short supply here.

171
00:05:52,780 --> 00:05:54,900
会有一群工于心计的狐狸精
And a lot of scheming harpies will swoop in

172
00:05:54,900 --> 00:05:56,300
在你父亲尚未察觉的情况下蜂拥而至
before your father knows what hit him.

173
00:05:56,840 --> 00:05:57,560
我爱弗兰克
I love Frank,

174
00:05:57,560 --> 00:05:59,020
但任何会做饭的女人都能牵着他鼻子走"
but he'll follow anything with a casserole."

175
00:05:59,080 --> 00:06:00,360
我真觉得难以置信
I don't believe this.

176
00:06:00,640 --> 00:06:01,540
这也太快了
It's too soon,

177
00:06:01,540 --> 00:06:03,000
何况我爸又不是动画片里的熊熊
and my dad's not a cartoon bear.

178
00:06:03,020 --> 00:06:05,460
他有足够的能力作出理智的判断
He's perfectly capable of making intelligent decisions.

179
00:06:05,760 --> 00:06:07,480
爸妈 我做了饼干
Hey, guys? I made cookies.

180
00:06:07,740 --> 00:06:09,040
太好了 我还以为是邻居家做的
Oh, good. I thought that was a neighbor.

181
00:06:14,660 --> 00:06:17,600
孩子们 奶奶给你们每个人留了些东西
Hey, kids, your grandma left each of you something.

182
00:06:17,600 --> 00:06:19,140
太棒了 是乐步鞋
Cool! Rockports!

183
00:06:19,140 --> 00:06:20,040
只是用了鞋盒子而已
It's just the box.

184
00:06:21,920 --> 00:06:23,420
我的天 有一封信
oh, my god. There's a letter.

185
00:06:23,600 --> 00:06:24,980
我觉得我还没做好心理准备
I don't know if I'm ready for this.

186
00:06:25,180 --> 00:06:26,140
尽管如果这是奶奶写的
Although if grandma wrote it,

187
00:06:26,140 --> 00:06:27,100
她一定事先感觉到我已经准备好了
she must have sensed I was ready.

188
00:06:27,180 --> 00:06:28,600
因为你俩有特殊的感情纽带吗
Because you had such a bond?

189
00:06:28,979 --> 00:06:29,832
你也感觉到了吗
You felt it, too?

190
00:06:29,843 --> 00:06:31,454
海莉 跟我们说说你那封信的内容
Haley, why don't you tell us what yours says?

191
00:06:31,454 --> 00:06:32,729
写得真贴心
Well, it's so sweet.

192
00:06:32,729 --> 00:06:35,120
是关于我的内在是多么美丽 还有
It's about how beautiful I am inside and--

193
00:06:35,120 --> 00:06:35,900
帅啊 首饰
Score! Jewelry

194
00:06:37,400 --> 00:06:38,320
快来看
Check it out!

195
00:06:38,320 --> 00:06:39,207
看看
Oh, look at that.

196
00:06:39,360 --> 00:06:40,780
你奶奶可喜欢怀表了
Your grandma loved pocket watches.

197
00:06:40,780 --> 00:06:42,520
她说过怀表让人看起来很高贵
Aw! She said they made a man look dignified.

198
00:06:42,520 --> 00:06:44,260
这条链子是为了防止有人吞下它吗
Is this chain in case you swallow it?

199
00:06:44,540 --> 00:06:45,900
不是 但我突然好庆幸有这条链子
No, but suddenly I'm glad it's there.

200
00:06:46,120 --> 00:06:48,460
-打火机 -信里怎么说
- A lighter? - Huh. What does the note say?

201
00:06:50,500 --> 00:06:51,600
"这是一个打火机"
"This is a lighter."

202
00:06:52,660 --> 00:06:54,020
我不明白
I don't understand.

203
00:06:54,440 --> 00:06:56,040
你还要她说得多清楚呢
How much clearer could she have been?

204
00:06:56,260 --> 00:06:57,780
我觉得你不要想太多了
I wouldn't read too much into it.

205
00:06:57,820 --> 00:06:59,120
奶奶一直很爱你们
Your grandma loved you very much.

206
00:06:59,140 --> 00:07:01,760
她只是在生命最后做了些奇怪的事情
She just did a couple of bizarre things towards the end.

207
00:07:02,620 --> 00:07:04,320
艾丽克斯 我可以帮你
Here, Alex, I can help you out with that.

208
00:07:05,000 --> 00:07:06,800
你现在很困很困想睡觉
You are getting very sleepy.

209
00:07:07,300 --> 00:07:09,800
破烂旧打火机并不是个很糟的礼物
A crappy old lighter is not a sucky gift.

210
00:07:09,800 --> 00:07:13,520
亲爱的 你不打算完成你妈妈的遗嘱吗
Honey, hey, hey. So you're not gonna do what your mom asked?

211
00:07:13,520 --> 00:07:15,140
在她葬礼这天把我爸
Marry off my dad to a complete stranger

212
00:07:15,140 --> 00:07:16,840
许配给一个陌生人吗 我想不会
on the day of her funeral? I think not.

213
00:07:17,000 --> 00:07:18,180
这可是她的遗愿
It was her last wish.

214
00:07:18,300 --> 00:07:19,360
等我爸准备好了
When my dad is ready,

215
00:07:19,560 --> 00:07:20,900
他会去挑他喜欢的女友
he gets to pick his own girlfriend.

216
00:07:20,980 --> 00:07:22,480
这可是妻子去世的一大好处
That's the big upside to your wife dying.

217
00:07:24,180 --> 00:07:25,920
再就是 以后说话不用脑子也没事了
Also, not having to think before you speak.

218
00:07:26,160 --> 00:07:26,480
是啊
Yeah.

219
00:07:28,220 --> 00:07:30,240
法官阁下 这一切都归结于此
Your honor, it all boils down to this.

220
00:07:30,240 --> 00:07:32,403
这家旅馆欠"曼查勾"小姐的
The motel owes Miss Menchengo--

221
00:07:32,413 --> 00:07:33,826
-曼查卡 -该死 每次都错
- Menchaca. - Damn it. Every time.

222
00:07:33,826 --> 00:07:35,960
薪水高于她拿走的
more in wages than she ever could've taken

223
00:07:35,960 --> 00:07:38,280
香皂和超小瓶洗发水的价值
in soaps and tiny shampoos.

224
00:07:38,540 --> 00:07:39,920
好吧 案件驳回
Fine. Case dismissed.

225
00:07:39,920 --> 00:07:40,780
太好了
Yes!

226
00:07:41,955 --> 00:07:43,633
谢谢 太谢谢了
Oh! Gracias! Muchas gracias!

227
00:07:43,633 --> 00:07:45,120
-不客气 不客气 -太谢谢了
- De nada. De nada. - Muchas gracias.

228
00:07:45,120 --> 00:07:47,200
看见没 我胜诉了
Did you see that? I won!

229
00:07:47,200 --> 00:07:48,960
-真是不敢相信 -看到了
- I-I can't believe it! - Yeah.

230
00:07:48,960 --> 00:07:51,200
你赢一次这么高兴 我很怕你胜诉率很低
It scares me that winning is such a surprise for you.

231
00:07:51,500 --> 00:07:55,080
下一个 马修·普乐斯科 违规停车
Next! Matthew Plonsker. Parking violations.

232
00:07:55,400 --> 00:07:57,980
我还以为会有点生疏 但显然没有
I thought I'd be a little rusty, but apparently not.

233
00:07:59,420 --> 00:08:01,400
又来找我吗 真"好"呢
Oh! Really? Sweet.

234
00:08:01,880 --> 00:08:03,820
去吧 把错误都犯在他身上
Yes! Go make your mistakes with him.

235
00:08:03,820 --> 00:08:05,700
我可不想因为卖淫坐牢
I don't want to go to jail for prostitution.

236
00:08:08,541 --> 00:08:10,222
你以为你能嫖得起我吗
Like you could afford me.

237
00:08:10,680 --> 00:08:12,360
在我看来 在那个重要的下午
It seems to me it wasn't only the meter

238
00:08:12,360 --> 00:08:14,840
并不只是停车计费表坏了
that was broken that fateful afternoon.

239
00:08:15,180 --> 00:08:15,460
不仅如此
Nay!

240
00:08:16,120 --> 00:08:18,780
是整个刑事司法系统坏了
It was the entire criminal justice system.

241
00:08:19,320 --> 00:08:21,040
因此我要提出的是
Therefore I submit to you,

242
00:08:21,040 --> 00:08:23,940
那晚影响我的客户判断力的唯一一样东西
the only "Influence" my client was under that night

243
00:08:23,940 --> 00:08:25,680
就是他对划船的热爱
was his love of boating.

244
00:08:27,780 --> 00:08:28,260
可耻啊
Shame!

245
00:08:31,260 --> 00:08:33,540
我只是不懂 她为什么给我一个打火机
I just don't get it. Why would she give me a lighter?

246
00:08:33,540 --> 00:08:35,800
也许她希望你把你所有丑衣服都烧掉
Maybe she wants you to burn all your clothes.

247
00:08:36,640 --> 00:08:38,780
是不是我们并不像我想的那样有特殊的感情纽带
Is it possible we didn't have the connection I thought we did?

248
00:08:39,225 --> 00:08:41,418
我不知道 你也听老爸说了
I don't know. You heard dad.

249
00:08:41,700 --> 00:08:43,580
她去世前一直在接受药物治疗
She was on all that medication towards the end.

250
00:08:43,680 --> 00:08:45,600
人们服药期间总会做些诡异的事
People do weird things when they're on drugs.

251
00:08:46,040 --> 00:08:48,140
迪兰在牙根管治疗后服了止痛药
When Dylan was on vicodin after his root canal,

252
00:08:48,140 --> 00:08:51,200
他买了一整套《女医生》光盘
he bought the complete DVD set of "Dr. Quinn Medicine Woman."

253
00:08:54,880 --> 00:08:55,920
女孩们 请离开
Get going, ladies.

254
00:08:55,920 --> 00:08:57,160
泳池只对当地居民开放
The pool's for residents only.

255
00:08:57,300 --> 00:08:58,600
好的 对不起 我们这就走
Oh, okay. Sorry. We'll leave.

256
00:08:58,600 --> 00:09:00,734
不 我们不走 这里又没人
Uh, no, we won't. There's nobody here.

257
00:09:00,734 --> 00:09:02,729
-海莉 -为什么我们不能用这泳池
- Haley! - Why can't we use the pool?

258
00:09:02,740 --> 00:09:04,060
这是规定
Because those are the rules.

259
00:09:04,255 --> 00:09:06,080
有什么问题吗
Are we gonna have a problem here?

260
00:09:06,080 --> 00:09:08,880
你可吓不着我 我蹲过真正的监狱
You don't scare me. I've been in real jail.

261
00:09:09,440 --> 00:09:11,440
你俩是聪明人 不是吗
Oh, you two are pretty smart, aren't you?

262
00:09:11,580 --> 00:09:13,820
不 只有她聪明
No. Only she is.

263
00:09:18,280 --> 00:09:18,880
北风
North.

264
00:09:19,240 --> 00:09:19,820
花牌
Flowers.

265
00:09:20,480 --> 00:09:20,980
红中
Red.

266
00:09:22,480 --> 00:09:23,200
一筒
One dot.

267
00:09:24,200 --> 00:09:24,900
二条
Two bam.

268
00:09:26,635 --> 00:09:27,974
我和了
I have mahj!

269
00:09:27,993 --> 00:09:29,560
-嘻嘻 -你又和了
- Hee hee! - Again?!

270
00:09:29,778 --> 00:09:31,721
你今天手气真好啊 伊迪丝
Wow, you're really on some streak, Edith.

271
00:09:31,880 --> 00:09:33,260
走牌运啊
Luck of the tiles.

272
00:09:33,940 --> 00:09:35,620
还有人要来点潘趣酒吗
Anyone else want some punch?

273
00:09:36,660 --> 00:09:37,980
好啊 我也来点
Yeah. I'll join you.

274
00:09:42,280 --> 00:09:44,240
你打得真不错
You are very good.

275
00:09:44,700 --> 00:09:46,680
你这样的农场男孩是在哪里学的麻将
Where'd a farm boy like you learn to play mahjong?

276
00:09:46,691 --> 00:09:48,146
在一个夏天
Oh, well, one summer,

277
00:09:48,146 --> 00:09:50,020
我在中央密苏里圣约之子会工作
I worked at the Central Missouri b'nai b'rith.

278
00:09:50,020 --> 00:09:51,820
是全国最小的分会
It's the nation's smallest chapter.

279
00:09:52,620 --> 00:09:53,660
听我说 玛丽莲
Listen, Marilyn,

280
00:09:53,720 --> 00:09:55,720
我不想挑拨离间的
I don't mean to stir things up,

281
00:09:55,780 --> 00:09:59,740
但我看到伊迪丝从她口袋里拿了那张吊牌
But I just saw Edith take the winning tile out of her jacket pocket.

282
00:09:59,740 --> 00:10:01,600
我就知道
I knew it!

283
00:10:01,900 --> 00:10:02,840
没人会手气那么好
Nobody's that good!

284
00:10:02,980 --> 00:10:04,120
我也跟你一样震惊
Listen, I'm as shocked as you are.

285
00:10:04,120 --> 00:10:05,920
只是伊迪丝看上去不是那种人
It just doesn't seem like Edith.

286
00:10:05,980 --> 00:10:08,900
是 就是这样 知人知面不知心
Yeah, well, it goes to show, you think you know someone...

287
00:10:16,120 --> 00:10:17,820
饼干都去哪里了
What happened to all the cookies?

288
00:10:18,260 --> 00:10:20,620
我真的不想挑拨离间的
Oh, well, you know I hate to stir things up...

289
00:10:24,040 --> 00:10:25,420
-抱歉 -什么事
- Excuse me. - Yes?

290
00:10:25,540 --> 00:10:26,340
我是杰·普里契特
Jay Pritchett.

291
00:10:26,620 --> 00:10:28,600
弗兰克·邓菲是我亲家
Frank Dunphy's son is married to my daughter.

292
00:10:28,600 --> 00:10:29,840
真是遗憾
Oh, I'm so sorry.

293
00:10:30,080 --> 00:10:31,400
他那套幽默果然会传染身边人
Ah, he grows on you.

294
00:10:31,700 --> 00:10:33,500
你是说很遗憾我亲家母过世 谢谢关心
Oh, you're talking about the death. Thank you.

295
00:10:33,880 --> 00:10:37,580
我看你非常脸熟 你在俄亥俄生活过吗
You look very familiar to me. Did you ever live in Ohio?

296
00:10:39,000 --> 00:10:40,860
没 我是彭萨科拉人
No. I'm from Pensacola.

297
00:10:41,580 --> 00:10:42,760
然后我突然就想到了
And then it hit me.

298
00:10:42,860 --> 00:10:45,600
我新兵入伍时 在彭萨科拉受过训
I had done my basic training in Pensacola.

299
00:10:45,960 --> 00:10:47,180
她是我的初夜
She was my first.

300
00:10:47,620 --> 00:10:49,180
我永远忘不了她 夏洛特什么的
I'll never forget her-- Charlotte somebody.

301
00:10:49,520 --> 00:10:51,700
我当年18岁 她31岁
I was 18, and she was 31.

302
00:10:51,740 --> 00:10:54,200
我们当时爱得死去活来
And we fell pretty hard for each other.

303
00:10:54,680 --> 00:10:56,200
我从越战回来后就再没联系她
I always felt bad I never called her

304
00:10:56,200 --> 00:10:57,560
心里一直很难受
when I got back from Vietnam.

305
00:10:57,560 --> 00:11:00,840
尤其是因为当时我已经 你懂的
Especially because by then I had, you know...

306
00:11:00,840 --> 00:11:01,820
已经开拓了新的眼界
learned a few things.

307
00:11:02,580 --> 00:11:04,300
不好意思 请你谅解
I'm sorry. You'll have to forgive me.

308
00:11:04,300 --> 00:11:05,920
我岁数大了 记性不好了
My memory isn't what it used to be.

309
00:11:05,940 --> 00:11:08,680
我当时在海军 杰·普里契特
I was in the navy. Jay Pritchett.

310
00:11:09,460 --> 00:11:10,360
当年头发多些
Little more up here,

311
00:11:11,020 --> 00:11:11,760
赘肉少些
little less down here.

312
00:11:11,820 --> 00:11:13,480
我敢说你一定是个好男人
I'm sure you're a very nice man,

313
00:11:13,480 --> 00:11:16,540
但我觉得你把我错认成别人了
but I-I think you may have mistaken me for someone else.

314
00:11:16,660 --> 00:11:18,080
我当时就快要被派往越南
I was shipping off to vietnam.

315
00:11:18,080 --> 00:11:19,838
你当年的屁股就跟年轻女星安·玛格丽特一样
You had the ass of a young Ann Margret.

316
00:11:19,940 --> 00:11:21,020
好吧 那确实是我
Yeah, that was me.

317
00:11:22,260 --> 00:11:23,760
这张照片里奶奶真高兴
Grandma looks so happy here.

318
00:11:24,720 --> 00:11:26,340
是啊 当时我们喝得烂醉
Yeah. We were pretty hammered.

319
00:11:27,575 --> 00:11:30,391
那是去年的国庆节 你奶奶最喜欢的节日
That was last 4th of July-- grandma's favorite holiday.

320
00:11:31,280 --> 00:11:32,660
普林朴顿家搞了烧烤
The Plimptons had a barbecue,

321
00:11:32,669 --> 00:11:35,099
你奶奶和我喝姜汁玛格丽特喝多了
and Gram and I got a little tipsy on ginger margaritas.

322
00:11:35,099 --> 00:11:37,042
我们就回家打了个盹
We came home for a catnap

323
00:11:37,180 --> 00:11:39,760
结果错过了那晚的烟花表演
and slept right through the big fireworks show.

324
00:11:40,160 --> 00:11:41,580
她头一回错过
First one she ever missed.

325
00:11:42,060 --> 00:11:43,080
她当时特别生气
Boy, was she mad.

326
00:11:43,580 --> 00:11:44,640
我为了补偿她
I made it up to her

327
00:11:44,640 --> 00:11:46,500
当天晚些时候特意为她办了一场烟火表演
with a little fireworks show of our own later.

328
00:11:46,760 --> 00:11:47,260
爷爷
Grandpa!

329
00:11:47,880 --> 00:11:50,700
只是在后院用弹弓发射荧光棒而已
A couple of glow sticks and a slingshot in the backyard.

330
00:11:52,860 --> 00:11:55,240
但接下来的性爱值得我们回味一生
Which led to some pretty memorable lovemaking.

331
00:11:56,860 --> 00:11:58,840
我不是故意转移话题
Not to change the subject,

332
00:11:59,120 --> 00:12:01,360
但我真不懂奶奶送这个给我的意义
but I don't really get the gift grandma left me.

333
00:12:01,500 --> 00:12:03,080
她在信里没解释吗
Well, didn't she explain it in the note?

334
00:12:03,300 --> 00:12:05,060
没 信里就几个字
No. The note's four words.

335
00:12:06,480 --> 00:12:08,160
你知道这纸还要展开的吧
You know it opens, right?

336
00:12:08,660 --> 00:12:09,280
是吗
It does?

337
00:12:10,000 --> 00:12:13,460
当然 佛罗里达太潮湿了 东西都黏一块了
Sure. Look, it's Florida. Everything sticks together.

338
00:12:17,512 --> 00:12:18,753
真是太诡异了
It's all so weird.

339
00:12:19,580 --> 00:12:21,120
心里一直害怕面对的事
This thing you dread in the back of your mind

340
00:12:21,120 --> 00:12:22,300
突然就成真了
suddenly becomes real.

341
00:12:22,328 --> 00:12:23,215
我懂
I know.

342
00:12:24,140 --> 00:12:25,860
不过有你在 我感觉好多了
I feel better having you here, though.

343
00:12:26,080 --> 00:12:27,580
我会永远在你身边
Oh, I'm always here for you.

344
00:12:28,600 --> 00:12:29,520
看那房子
Look at that house.

345
00:12:29,940 --> 00:12:31,000
真漂亮啊
That is a cute house.

346
00:12:31,220 --> 00:12:32,480
我想知道谁住这儿
I wonder who lives there.

347
00:12:33,160 --> 00:12:33,920
我不知道
I don't know.

348
00:12:35,440 --> 00:12:36,860
克莱尔 你要干嘛
Claire, what are you doing?

349
00:12:37,100 --> 00:12:38,340
我喜欢这房子
I love this house.

350
00:12:38,480 --> 00:12:40,360
我敢肯定不管是谁住这儿 我都会喜欢那人
I bet you anything I would love whoever lives here.

351
00:12:40,440 --> 00:12:41,040
等等
Wait a minute.

352
00:12:41,040 --> 00:12:42,960
我妈信上说的人就住这儿 是吧
That lady from my mom's letter lives here,doesn't she?

353
00:12:43,020 --> 00:12:43,820
安妮·菲茨曼斯
Annie Fitzsimmons.

354
00:12:44,160 --> 00:12:45,220
菲尔 听我说
Phil, listen to me.

355
00:12:45,560 --> 00:12:47,640
你也许有理由不想这么做
You may have your reasons for not wanting to do this,

356
00:12:47,720 --> 00:12:50,100
但你母亲是个很英明的女人
but your mother was a very wise woman.

357
00:12:50,100 --> 00:12:52,560
她相信这扇门背后的那个人
She believed that whoever is behind that door

358
00:12:52,560 --> 00:12:55,220
能让你父亲拥有幸福的余生
would make your father happy for the rest of his life.

359
00:12:57,360 --> 00:12:58,480
你们好 有事吗
Yeah. What can I do for you?

360
00:12:59,080 --> 00:12:59,900
她真"完美"
She's perfect.

361
00:13:00,620 --> 00:13:02,000
我以为安妮·菲茨曼斯住这儿
I thought Annie Fitzsimmons lived here.

362
00:13:02,120 --> 00:13:04,100
是的 安妮 亲爱的
She does. Annie, honey!

363
00:13:04,111 --> 00:13:05,836
有人想见你
There's people here to see ya!

364
00:13:06,360 --> 00:13:07,560
-你好 -你好
- Hi. - Hi.

365
00:13:07,880 --> 00:13:08,720
有事吗
Can I help you?

366
00:13:09,520 --> 00:13:10,780
我们是推销吸尘器的
We're selling vacuum cleaners.

367
00:13:11,320 --> 00:13:12,540
那可真奇怪
That is strange.

368
00:13:12,720 --> 00:13:13,280
我知道
I know.

369
00:13:13,280 --> 00:13:15,760
因为我家吸尘器早上正好坏了
Because just this morning, my vacuum cleaner broke.

370
00:13:15,920 --> 00:13:18,200
都怪我 我的体毛脱落像牧羊犬那么多
That's on me. I shed like a collie.

371
00:13:18,640 --> 00:13:19,740
我看看你们的货
Let's see what you got.

372
00:13:19,740 --> 00:13:21,060
对啊 克莱尔 来看看你的货
Yes, Claire, let's see what you got.

373
00:13:21,720 --> 00:13:22,720
我没带来
I didn't bring it.

374
00:13:22,780 --> 00:13:23,840
-你没带 -是的
- You didn't bring it? - No.

375
00:13:23,900 --> 00:13:25,880
我们出门时你还带着的啊
You had it when we left the vacuum cleaner office.

376
00:13:26,160 --> 00:13:28,600
我看这下你要好好认错了
I guess it's fair to say you've made a huge mistake.

377
00:13:29,940 --> 00:13:31,620
不行 要说出来
No. Say it.

378
00:13:31,780 --> 00:13:33,540
我也不想为难她 可这就是培训
I'm sorry to do that. It's part of the training.

379
00:13:34,460 --> 00:13:36,120
我犯了个大错
I've made a huge mistake.

380
00:13:37,842 --> 00:13:39,669
我觉得她是不适合干这行的
I don't think she's gonna work out.

381
00:13:45,697 --> 00:13:48,218
-我又和了 -真厉害
- That's mahj again! - Oh! Well, shocker.

382
00:13:48,260 --> 00:13:50,300
-够了 你出老千 -我没有
- That's it. You're cheating. - I am not.

383
00:13:50,480 --> 00:13:52,700
得了吧 你藏的牌
Oh, please! You've stashed more tiles

384
00:13:52,700 --> 00:13:54,565
比玛丽莲藏的饼干还多
than Marilyn has cookies!

385
00:13:55,106 --> 00:13:56,780
好了 大家先歇歇
O-okay. Uh, let's just take a breath.

386
00:13:56,780 --> 00:13:58,580
谁在乎麻将牌啊 饼干啊
Who cares about tiles or cookies

387
00:13:58,580 --> 00:14:00,500
或者海蒂偷偷往她的咖啡里倒的什东西
Or whatever Hattie's slipping into her coffee?

388
00:14:00,620 --> 00:14:02,340
我就知道你又开始酗酒了
I knew you were drinking again!

389
00:14:02,360 --> 00:14:03,560
她的驾照就是这么被吊销的
That's how she lost her license.

390
00:14:03,580 --> 00:14:04,820
闭上你们的臭嘴
You shut your traps!

391
00:14:04,820 --> 00:14:05,789
-去死吧 -去你的
- Drop dead! - Screw you!

392
00:14:05,789 --> 00:14:06,672
-你也是 -女士们
- Yeah, you, too! Ladies.

393
00:14:06,681 --> 00:14:08,001
-你也是 -女士们
- And you! - Ladies.

394
00:14:08,239 --> 00:14:09,720
别说了 别吵了
Stop it! You--stop it.

395
00:14:09,720 --> 00:14:11,580
你们都当了20年的闺蜜了
You have been friends for 20 years.

396
00:14:11,900 --> 00:14:14,540
你们这是怎么回事啊
What on earth has gotten into you all?

397
00:14:15,740 --> 00:14:18,920
为什么我到哪都会碰上极品事呢
Why does drama keep following me everywhere I go?

398
00:14:18,920 --> 00:14:20,980
总是无缘无故就冒一出
It just keeps popping up out of nowhere.

399
00:14:21,261 --> 00:14:22,766
跟克里斯宾脑袋上冒出来的头发似的
like Crispin's hair plugs.

400
00:14:23,920 --> 00:14:25,740
然后我们去了你的公寓
And so we went to your apartment.

401
00:14:26,460 --> 00:14:27,580
到现在我还是觉得很丢人
It's still embarrassing.

402
00:14:27,840 --> 00:14:29,680
我当时告诉你我从没跟女人做过
I told you I had never been with a woman.

403
00:14:30,340 --> 00:14:32,960
你牵着我的手 带我进了卧室
And you took me by the hand and you led me into the bedroom.

404
00:14:32,960 --> 00:14:34,921
你是那么温柔美丽
You were so sweet and beautiful.

405
00:14:35,400 --> 00:14:36,540
那一刻我感觉自己到了天堂
I thought I'd gone to heaven.

406
00:14:37,980 --> 00:14:40,360
-杰·普里契特 -是我 就是我
- Jay pritchett. - Yes! Yes!

407
00:14:40,980 --> 00:14:42,220
我想起来了
I remember that.

408
00:14:42,580 --> 00:14:43,720
你那会可真帅呀
You were so handsome.

409
00:14:44,220 --> 00:14:45,040
我可不敢说自己帅
I don't know about that.

410
00:14:45,040 --> 00:14:45,965
可能还算讨人喜欢
I mean, cute, maybe.

411
00:14:45,965 --> 00:14:47,283
是常有人夸我的眼睛迷人来着
I--people talk about my eyes.

412
00:14:47,520 --> 00:14:52,560
我一直很后悔回来后没再联系你
But I always regretted not getting in touch with you when I got back,

413
00:14:52,560 --> 00:14:54,300
因为你带给我的美好回忆
Because you had given me something

414
00:14:54,300 --> 00:14:57,080
我已经珍惜了差不多50年了
that I cherished for almost 50 years.

415
00:14:57,420 --> 00:14:59,360
你也给了我些东西
You gave me something, too.

416
00:14:59,800 --> 00:15:00,400
是吗
I did?

417
00:15:00,760 --> 00:15:02,080
你在这儿乖乖等着
You wait right there.

418
00:15:02,940 --> 00:15:04,360
我去那是为了参加一个葬礼
I'm down there for a funeral--

419
00:15:04,360 --> 00:15:05,907
原本是很悲伤的一件事
It's such a sad event--

420
00:15:06,260 --> 00:15:09,180
我却找到了本以为已经永远失去了的东西
And I end up finding something that I thought was lost forever.

421
00:15:09,260 --> 00:15:10,900
当年那美妙的"小插曲"
This beautiful moment

422
00:15:10,900 --> 00:15:12,860
对我们都有着难以取代的意义
that meant so much to both of us,

423
00:15:13,160 --> 00:15:14,900
尤其是在反击越共的时代大背景下
set against the backdrop of fighting commies.

424
00:15:15,820 --> 00:15:17,020
简直能拍部电影啊
There's your movie.

425
00:15:17,440 --> 00:15:21,080
我清楚地记得你把这东西给我时我在哪儿
I remember exactly where I was when you gave it to me.

426
00:15:21,843 --> 00:15:23,340
你当时说"戴上这个手..."
You said, "Wear this bec--"

427
00:15:23,340 --> 00:15:24,840
不 这不是我的
No, no. This isn't mine.

428
00:15:24,900 --> 00:15:26,540
我从来没上过杰弗逊高中
And I never went to Jefferson High.

429
00:15:27,320 --> 00:15:29,120
噢 是我搞错了
Oh. My mistake.

430
00:15:30,000 --> 00:15:30,960
是这个
Here it is.

431
00:15:31,711 --> 00:15:32,960
-你当时说"戴上这个..." -不对不对
- You said, "Pin this--" - No, no. N-no.

432
00:15:32,960 --> 00:15:34,160
我从来没得过什么奖牌
Never got a medal.

433
00:15:34,868 --> 00:15:35,639
而且...
And, uh...

434
00:15:36,320 --> 00:15:38,200
我参的也不是这支军
This is the wrong branch of service.

435
00:15:38,940 --> 00:15:39,640
当然了
Of course.

436
00:15:40,960 --> 00:15:42,280
这些是...
These are th--

437
00:15:42,280 --> 00:15:42,760
从没写过信
Never wrote.

438
00:15:45,080 --> 00:15:47,060
你要不自己找吧
Why don't you look through here?

439
00:15:47,960 --> 00:15:49,520
原来她送上战场的军人
Turns out she sent more men off to war

440
00:15:49,520 --> 00:15:50,780
比林顿·约翰逊还要多
than Lyndon Johnson.

441
00:15:52,580 --> 00:15:53,320
到家了
Well, we're here.

442
00:15:53,320 --> 00:15:55,060
你要不要试试向我爸推销个吸尘器
You wanna try to sell my dad a vacuum?

443
00:15:55,060 --> 00:15:56,180
你就嘲笑我吧
Tease me all you want.

444
00:15:56,220 --> 00:15:57,740
我很高兴至少我们试过了
I am glad that we at least tried.

445
00:15:57,840 --> 00:16:00,260
我知道你是好心 但他一个人也会过得很好
I know you mean well, but he's gonna be fine on his own.

446
00:16:00,595 --> 00:16:01,846
太好笑了
So funny.

447
00:16:02,669 --> 00:16:04,600
来 尝尝我做的 弗兰克
Ooh! Here. Try mine, Frank.

448
00:16:04,600 --> 00:16:05,720
我敢说一定很好吃
I bet it's delicious.

449
00:16:06,040 --> 00:16:07,460
除非你味觉挂了
If your taste buds are dead.

450
00:16:07,580 --> 00:16:08,960
"挂了" 你真会照顾别人的心情 米娜
Dead? Real sensitive, Myra.

451
00:16:08,960 --> 00:16:10,200
他妻子尸骨都未寒呢
The woman's not even cold...

452
00:16:10,240 --> 00:16:11,440
当然你的奶酪茄子是早凉了
unlike your eggplant parm.

453
00:16:11,520 --> 00:16:12,600
这演的是哪出
What is going on?

454
00:16:12,646 --> 00:16:15,280
鲨鱼群争食呢 你爸爸就是那可怜的食物
Oh, it's a feeding frenzy. They're all over him.

455
00:16:15,280 --> 00:16:17,080
她们还量了窗户的尺寸 想换新窗帘呢
They're practically measuring the windows for new drapes.

456
00:16:17,180 --> 00:16:17,860
真把我恶心坏了
It's disgusting.

457
00:16:18,000 --> 00:16:19,980
你一定要把这个食谱给我 米娜
I must get this recipe, Myra.

458
00:16:20,140 --> 00:16:20,780
当然
Oh, sure.

459
00:16:20,900 --> 00:16:23,040
你要那食谱吗 解冻 加热 端上来就行了
You want the recipe? It's thaw, heat, and serve.

460
00:16:23,040 --> 00:16:26,260
我妈妈说得对 她们会把他生吞了
My mom was right. They're gonna eat him alive.

461
00:16:26,260 --> 00:16:27,340
你觉得我们有能力拆散
Do you think we can break up

462
00:16:27,340 --> 00:16:28,700
安妮·菲茨曼斯和她男朋友吗
Annie fitzsimmons and her boyfriend?

463
00:16:29,080 --> 00:16:29,520
男朋友
Boyfriend?

464
00:16:29,880 --> 00:16:31,780
你是说马维 哎呀妈 太好笑了
Oh, you mean Marv? Oh, that's hilarious.

465
00:16:32,520 --> 00:16:34,560
马维是她哥哥 从庞帕诺来玩的
Marv's her brother, visiting from Pompano.

466
00:16:34,720 --> 00:16:35,620
他仅仅是过来度周末的
he's here for the week,

467
00:16:35,620 --> 00:16:37,646
这地方一半的女人都跟他有一腿
Slept with half the women in this place.

468
00:16:37,707 --> 00:16:39,428
她现在单身 真是太棒了
She's single? This is fantastic.

469
00:16:39,428 --> 00:16:40,660
小卡 你都是打哪知道的
Cam, how do you know that?

470
00:16:40,660 --> 00:16:42,120
这地方的八卦简直满天飞
This place is lousy with gossips.

471
00:16:44,040 --> 00:16:45,600
下一个 歌洛莉亚·迪尔加多
Next. Gloria Delgado?

472
00:16:45,820 --> 00:16:46,480
我在这儿
I'm here!

473
00:16:47,260 --> 00:16:50,020
协同卖淫罪 你打算怎么辩护
Conspiring to promote prostitution. How do you plead?

474
00:16:50,220 --> 00:16:53,000
-无罪 法官大人 -老天 又是你
-Not guilty, your honor. - Oh, good. It's you.

475
00:16:53,180 --> 00:16:55,960
陛下 我什么坏事都没干
Your Majesty, I didn't do anything wrong.

476
00:16:56,100 --> 00:16:58,040
但我愿意认罪
But I will say that I am guilty

477
00:16:58,040 --> 00:17:00,100
如果交了罚金就能让我回家的话
if I can just pay the fine and go home.

478
00:17:00,200 --> 00:17:01,180
不 你不能
No, you won't.

479
00:17:01,420 --> 00:17:03,060
你是清白的 我能证明这点
You're innocent, and I can prove it.

480
00:17:03,060 --> 00:17:05,380
法官大人 这份文件表明
Your honor, this document here shows

481
00:17:05,380 --> 00:17:08,220
我的当事人当时正住在加利福尼亚
that my client was a resident of California at the time.

482
00:17:08,220 --> 00:17:09,980
这些已兑支票表明
And these canceled checks prove

483
00:17:09,980 --> 00:17:12,500
她合法转租了本案所指的那套公寓
that she was legally subletting the apartment in question.

484
00:17:13,100 --> 00:17:15,540
我这人挺单纯的 但我知道一件事
I might be a simple man, but I do know one thing...

485
00:17:16,160 --> 00:17:17,780
如果狗不吠
if a dog don't bark--

486
00:17:17,780 --> 00:17:19,280
够了 我再也不想听他扯犊子了
Okay, I can't listen to him anymore.

487
00:17:19,660 --> 00:17:22,020
此案驳回 休庭
Case dismissed. Court adjourned.

488
00:17:22,481 --> 00:17:24,887
谢谢你 米奇尔 你太厉害了
Gracias, Mitchell! You're wonderful!

489
00:17:25,820 --> 00:17:27,060
其实 算我们走运
You know what? We got lucky

490
00:17:27,060 --> 00:17:29,140
"狗不吠"那句我都不知道怎么往下接
because I had no ending to that dog thing.

491
00:17:29,460 --> 00:17:31,560
如果你下周不忙的话
If you don't have anything to do next week,

492
00:17:31,580 --> 00:17:33,720
也许可以陪我去趟德州
maybe you can go with me to Texas.

493
00:17:36,120 --> 00:17:36,760
再次打扰
Hello again.

494
00:17:36,900 --> 00:17:38,580
不是吧 你一个人
Oh, no. You're alone.

495
00:17:38,860 --> 00:17:40,660
你炒掉了那个可爱姑娘吗
Did you fire that nice girl?

496
00:17:40,780 --> 00:17:43,260
不 她不是什么可爱姑娘 她是我老婆
No. She's not a nice girl. She's my wife.

497
00:17:43,260 --> 00:17:44,680
我们也不是卖吸尘器的
And we don't sell vacuums.

498
00:17:44,860 --> 00:17:46,400
谢天谢地 否则你们会饿死的
Thank god. You'd starve.

499
00:17:47,928 --> 00:17:49,890
其实我是菲尔·邓菲
I-I-I'm actually Phil Dunphy.

500
00:17:49,890 --> 00:17:51,980
我是弗兰克和格蕾丝·邓菲的儿子
I-I'm Frank and Grace Dunphy's son.

501
00:17:51,980 --> 00:17:54,840
我听说了你母亲去世的事 太遗憾了
Oh, I heard about your mom. I'm--I'm so sorry.

502
00:17:54,860 --> 00:17:55,360
谢谢
Thank you.

503
00:17:55,600 --> 00:17:57,300
我只见过她几次
I only met her a few times,

504
00:17:57,300 --> 00:17:59,660
但她看起来是个非常好的人
but she seemed like a lovely woman.

505
00:18:00,720 --> 00:18:02,580
但我还是不太明白你的来意
but I'm still confused.

506
00:18:03,060 --> 00:18:06,740
也许我的解释只会令你更困惑 但是
Well, this probably won't help, but, um...

507
00:18:07,980 --> 00:18:12,220
她的遗愿就是叫我撮合你和我爸
Her last request was for me to fix you up with my dad.

508
00:18:13,060 --> 00:18:13,860
我的天
Oh, my.

509
00:18:14,300 --> 00:18:16,800
是啊 我真希望自己是卖吸尘器的
Yeah. I really wish I sold vacuums.

510
00:18:17,540 --> 00:18:18,600
所以之前
So earlier...

511
00:18:18,600 --> 00:18:20,780
我们看到你哥哥来开门 十分震惊
We were thrown when your brother answered the door.

512
00:18:20,860 --> 00:18:21,960
我们以为他是你的男友
We thought he was your boyfriend.

513
00:18:22,600 --> 00:18:24,440
我不知道说什么好
I don't know what to say.

514
00:18:24,483 --> 00:18:27,883
是吗 我这个要求再正常不过了
Really? This is such a-a normal request I'm making.

515
00:18:28,120 --> 00:18:30,540
顺便说下 请不要感觉有任何压力
Please, by the way, don't feel pressured at all.

516
00:18:30,740 --> 00:18:32,240
我爸根本不知道这件事
My dad doesn't even know about this.

517
00:18:33,020 --> 00:18:35,440
但我必须告诉你 这是我母亲的遗愿
I-I just--I had to tell you. It's what she wanted.

518
00:18:36,040 --> 00:18:38,220
她总是会做这样疯狂的事
She was always doing crazy stuff like this...

519
00:18:38,220 --> 00:18:40,960
不遗余力地照顾我们
going out of her way to take care of us.

520
00:18:42,620 --> 00:18:44,060
有次我在电话里咳嗽
I coughed on the phone once,

521
00:18:44,060 --> 00:18:45,240
她就熬汤连夜快递给我
and she overnighted me soup.

522
00:18:45,840 --> 00:18:48,340
我想学滑雪 她就给我织毛衣
When I wanted to learn how to ski, she knit me a sweater.

523
00:18:50,000 --> 00:18:51,740
我想做海洋生物学家
When I wanted to be a marine biologist,

524
00:18:51,860 --> 00:18:53,780
她就给我织了件鲸鱼图案的毛衣
she knit me a sweater with a whale on it.

525
00:18:56,220 --> 00:18:57,580
谁会这样做啊
Who does that?

526
00:18:59,777 --> 00:19:01,683
她就是这样的人
That's just the kind of person she is.

527
00:19:02,200 --> 00:19:02,240
生前是
Was.

528
00:19:03,040 --> 00:19:04,080
亲爱的
Oh, sweetie.

529
00:19:06,260 --> 00:19:08,000
你是个好儿子
You're a good son.

530
00:19:09,820 --> 00:19:11,760
她说的对 你是个非常好的人
She was right. You are very nice.

531
00:19:23,660 --> 00:19:25,120
仪式太感人了
It's a beautiful service.

532
00:19:25,180 --> 00:19:27,440
让人思考要如何度过这一生
It really makes you think about how you wanna live your life.

533
00:19:28,540 --> 00:19:30,560
我想辞职 重返法庭
I wanna quit my job and get back into the courtroom.

534
00:19:30,760 --> 00:19:31,080
什么
What?

535
00:19:31,312 --> 00:19:33,620
先别对任何人说起这事
Just--just don't say anything to anyone.

536
00:19:33,620 --> 00:19:34,700
我能告诉谁啊
Well, who am I gonna tell?

537
00:19:36,673 --> 00:19:37,847
谢谢 梅尔
Thank you, Mel.

538
00:19:38,400 --> 00:19:39,420
你吹奏得很美
That was beautiful.

539
00:19:43,222 --> 00:19:44,940
在我们道晚安前
Um, before we say good night,

540
00:19:44,940 --> 00:19:47,280
我女儿艾丽克斯想致以悼念
my daughter Alex would like to pay tribute.

541
00:19:50,900 --> 00:19:51,720
谢谢 宝贝
Thanks, sweetie.

542
00:19:58,680 --> 00:20:01,500
奶奶和我有着特殊的感情纽带
My grandmother and I had a very special bond.

543
00:20:02,060 --> 00:20:02,940
不是吧 又来
Seriously? Again?

544
00:20:03,440 --> 00:20:05,160
也许大家不理解
This may not make sense to everyone,

545
00:20:05,754 --> 00:20:07,547
但我肯定 奶奶会喜欢的
but I'm pretty sure she would've loved it.

546
00:20:19,520 --> 00:20:20,720
"这是一个打火机
"This is a lighter.

547
00:20:21,799 --> 00:20:24,384
原本属于我最喜欢的演员 保罗·纽曼
It belonged to my favorite actor, Paul Newman.

548
00:20:24,740 --> 00:20:27,180
有一天 他来我做服务员的餐厅就餐
One day, he came into the restaurant where I was waitressing

549
00:20:27,180 --> 00:20:28,840
不小心落下了
and accidentally left it behind.

550
00:20:29,320 --> 00:20:31,240
我这辈子第一次
For the first time in my life,

551
00:20:31,240 --> 00:20:33,140
做了不应该做的事
I did something I wasn't supposed to

552
00:20:33,140 --> 00:20:34,440
将之据为己有
and slipped it into my pocket.

553
00:20:35,640 --> 00:20:37,080
有一位客人看到了
One of the customers saw

554
00:20:37,080 --> 00:20:39,460
说 "别担心 我会帮你保守秘密"
and said, 'don't worry. Your secret's safe with me.'

555
00:20:40,040 --> 00:20:42,860
那位客人后来成为了我的毕生挚爱
That customer turned out to be the love of my life,

556
00:20:43,020 --> 00:20:43,780
你的爷爷
your grandfather.

557
00:20:44,700 --> 00:20:47,120
所以 我最爱的艾丽克斯
So, my Alex, who I love so dearly,

558
00:20:47,120 --> 00:20:49,487
可能你太像我了 虽然这也挺好
who is probably too much like me for her own good,

559
00:20:50,340 --> 00:20:51,440
但偶尔的
every once in a while,

560
00:20:51,440 --> 00:20:53,220
不要害怕打破常规
don't be afraid to break the rules.

561
00:20:54,160 --> 00:20:55,600
你永远不知道会发生什么好事
You never know what can happen."

562
00:21:01,112 --> 00:21:02,217
天气怎么样
How 'bout this weather?

563
00:21:02,833 --> 00:21:05,261
还行 他们说要下雨了
Yep. They say it's supposed to rain.

564
00:21:05,500 --> 00:21:06,560
确实需要来场雨
We need it.

565
00:21:06,774 --> 00:21:07,702
穆丽尔
Muriel.

566
00:21:08,640 --> 00:21:10,680
你们两个收拾好准备走了吗
Are you two packed up and ready to go?

567
00:21:10,820 --> 00:21:11,120
是的
Yep.

568
00:21:13,000 --> 00:21:13,920
时间怎么过得这么快
Where does the time go?

569
00:21:14,660 --> 00:21:15,460
鬼才知道
Darned if I know.

570
00:21:15,860 --> 00:21:17,460
大家总是匆匆忙忙的
Everyone's always in such a hurry.

571
00:21:17,460 --> 00:21:20,180
何必如此 我们最后的归宿还不都一样
And why? We're all gonna end up in the same place.

572
00:21:21,950 --> 00:21:23,630
我觉得我们还是走吧
Well, I guess we better mosey.
